      "shortDescription": "Assistant Professor of Neurology, Harvard Medical School",
      "bio": "Alice Lam, MD PhD, is the principal investigator of the Lam Lab. She is a clinical neurologist and neuroscientist. Her clinical and translational research program explores the interface between epilepsy, the neurodegenerative diseases, and cognition. She uses a multimodal approach that leverages sophisticated techniques in clinical neurophysiology, machine learning, neuro-imaging, and neuropsychological testing.\n\nHer research is informed by clinical experience and inspired by her patients. She aims to improve the lives of people living with epilepsy, neurodegenerative diseases, or both.",
