      "shortDescription": "Instructor, Department of Neurology, Massachusetts General Hospital",
      "bio": "Dr. Alkis Hadjiosif joined MGH in July 2024 as a T32 research fellow. His work examines the mechanisms behind the different behavioral signs of post-stroke hemiparesis and how they interact with each other. The goal of this research is improving the assessment of hemiparesis and optimizing its rehabilitation. Alkis received his PhD in Bioengineering from Harvard University in 2015, and has been a research fellow at Johns Hopkins University and a research associate at Harvard University.",
